12. MOST ASKED INTERVIEW QUESTIONS
=========================================================


Q1. What problem does Facade solve?

Answer:

Facade provides a single entry point to multiple subsystems
and reduces complexity for the client.


---------------------------------------------------------


Q2. Why not allow client to call subsystem classes directly?


Answer:

Direct access increases coupling because client becomes
dependent on subsystem classes and their execution order.


---------------------------------------------------------


Q3. Does Facade change subsystem behavior?


Answer:

No.

Facade only coordinates subsystem operations.


---------------------------------------------------------


Q4. Does Facade use inheritance?


Answer:

No.

Facade mainly uses composition.

Relationship:

Facade HAS-A Subsystems


---------------------------------------------------------


Q5. Can subsystem classes be used without Facade?


Answer:

Yes.

Facade is optional.

Subsystem classes can still be accessed directly.


---------------------------------------------------------


Q6. Which SOLID principle does Facade support?


Mainly:

SRP (Single Responsibility Principle)

Because client does not handle subsystem coordination.


It can also support DIP when Facade exposes abstractions.


---------------------------------------------------------


13. FACADE vs ADAPTER
=========================================================


Facade:

- Simplifies complex subsystem
- Provides single entry point
- Hides complexity


Adapter:

- Converts one interface into another
- Makes incompatible classes work together
- Changes interface


Example:


Facade:

Client -> Facade -> Multiple Subsystems


Adapter:

Client -> Adapter -> Existing Class



---------------------------------------------------------


14. FACADE vs DECORATOR
=========================================================


Facade:

- Simplifies subsystem usage
- Provides one interface
- Coordinates multiple classes


Decorator:

- Adds new behavior dynamically
- Wraps an existing object
- Enhances functionality



---------------------------------------------------------


15. INTERVIEW ONE-LINER
=========================================================


Facade is a structural design pattern that provides a
simplified interface to a complex subsystem by hiding
internal details and reducing dependency between the client
and subsystem classes.



